Some days ago, someone asked for spoilers/tables concerning Nethack,
version 2.2.
This shell archive contains spoilers for NetHack, version 2.??. It is
the first of two archives. You should unpack this one first.

Subsequent information is found in the file Nethack/README.

#! /bin/sh
# This is a shell archive.  Remove anything before this line, then unpack
# it by saving it into a file and typing "sh file".  To overwrite existing
# files, type "sh file -c".  You can also feed this as standard input via
# unshar, or by typing "sh <file", e.g..  If this archive is complete, you
# will see the following message at the end:
#		"End of archive 1 (of 2)."
# Contents:  Nethack Nethack/README Nethack/Troff Nethack/Troff/armor
#   Nethack/Troff/characters Nethack/Troff/food
#   Nethack/Troff/fountains Nethack/Troff/gems Nethack/Troff/monfood1
#   Nethack/Troff/monfood2 Nethack/Troff/monsters1
#   Nethack/Troff/monsters2 Nethack/Troff/potions Nethack/Troff/rings
#   Nethack/Troff/scrolls Nethack/Troff/spellbooks
#   Nethack/Troff/thrones Nethack/Troff/tools Nethack/Troff/traps
#   Nethack/Troff/wands Nethack/Troff/weapons Nethack/plain_text
# Wrapped by wsbusup@eutrc3 (Boudewijn Wayers) on Fri Nov  3 13:41:32 1989
PATH=/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/ucb ; export PATH
if test ! -d 'Nethack' ; then
    echo shar: Creating directory \"'Nethack'\"
    mkdir 'Nethack'
fi
if test -f 'Nethack/README' -a "${1}" != "-c" ; then 
  echo shar: Will not clobber existing file \"'Nethack/README'\"
else
echo shar: Extracting \"'Nethack/README'\" \(1096 characters\)
sed "s/^X//" >'Nethack/README' <<'END_OF_FILE'
XNow you have unpacked this archive, you should have the following two
Xfiles:
X
Xplain_text	spoilers
X
X
XIn the subdirectory TROFF are 18 files containing tabelled information
Xabout NetHack (the PC-version 2.?? without many options).
X
XI once got this information and took the time to put it in Troff-format.
XI hope they don't contain too much errors.
X
XThe subsequent files are dealing with:
X
Xarmor		characters	food		fountains	gems
Xdead monsters (2 parts)		living monsters (2 parts)	potions
Xrings		scrolls		spells		thrones		tools
Xtraps		wands		weapons		
X
XYou can print them, using Troff (I don't know if Nroff will work too).
XNote: there might be some local macro's that I have used in the files.
X
X
XBy the way, I haven't played Nethack for a while, but keep reading this
Xnewsgroup.  I'm therefore NOT sure which version I've been playing, but
Xit didn't have sinks, stooges, or sacrifices yet.
X
X
XAnyway, good hacking!
X
X
Xwsbusr@eutrc3.UUCP  or:   ...!mcvax!eutrc3!wsbusr
X(Boudewijn Wayers @ Eindhoven University of Technology, the Netherlands)
X
X
XP.S. I will post these only once, and I won't email them!
END_OF_FILE
